{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369336379,"sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"todowrite","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-857cb16b656b5fac","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"todos":[{"content":"Create Flask app.py with routes, SQLite storage, validation","priority":"high","status":"in_progress"},{"content":"Create requirements.txt","priority":"medium","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write unit/integration tests (>=3)","priority":"high","status":"pending"},{"content":"Write README.md with setup/run instructions","priority":"medium","status":"pending"},{"content":"Run ruff lint, pytest, and verify build","priority":"high","status":"pending"}]},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Create Flask app.py with routes, SQLite storage, validation\",\n    \"status\": \"in_progress\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Create requirements.txt\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write unit/integration tests (>=3)\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Write README.md with setup/run instructions\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"medium\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"content\": \"Run ruff lint, pytest, and verify build\",\n    \"status\": \"pending\",\n    \"priority\": \"high\"\n  }\n]","metadata":{"todos":[{"content":"Create Flask app.py with routes, SQLite storage, validation","status":"in_progress","priority":"high"},{"content":"Create requirements.txt","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Write unit/integration tests (>=3)","status":"pending","priority":"high"},{"content":"Write README.md with setup/run instructions","status":"pending","priority":"medium"},{"content":"Run ruff lint, pytest, and verify build","status":"pending","priority":"high"}],"truncated":false},"title":"5 todos","time":{"start":1788369336372,"end":1788369336376}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Flask is installed. Now I'll build a REST API using Flask + SQLite. Let me plan the structure:\n\n- `app.py` - main Flask application with all routes and SQLite storage\n- `db.py` - database helper (or keep it in app.py)\n- `requirements.txt` - dependencies\n- `README.md` - setup and run instructions\n- `tests/` - tests\n\nLet me create a clean, well-structured Flask app. I'll use the application factory pattern for testability.\n\nLet me plan:\n1. `app.py` - application factory `create_app()`, routes, SQLite init\n2. `requirements.txt` - flask\n3. `README.md` - instructions\n4. `tests/test_books.py` - tests using Flask test client\n\nLet me create a todo list and start implementing.\n\nLet me design the app:\n\n- Database: SQLite stored in a file (or in-memory for tests). I'll use a config to point to the db path.\n- `init_db(db_path)` - creates the books table\n- Routes:\n  - GET /health -> {\"status\": \"ok\"}, 200\n  - POST /books -> create, 201 or 400\n  - GET /books -> list, support ?author= filter, 200\n  - GET /books/<id> -> 200 or 404\n  - PUT /books/<id> -> 200 or 404 or 400\n  - DELETE /books/<id> -> 204 or 404\n\nBook fields: id (auto), title (required), author (required), year (optional), isbn (optional)\n\nValidation: title and author required. year should be an integer if provided. Let me validate year is a valid integer and isbn is a string.\n\nLet me write the code. I'll use the application factory pattern with a config for the DB path so tests can use in-memory or temp file.\n\nLet me write app.py. I'll keep the DB logic clean with a helper module or inside app.py. Let me keep it all in app.py for simplicity, but make it testable.\n\nActually, let me structure it cleanly:\n- `app.py` contains `create_app(db_path=None)` and the routes.\n- For testing, use a temp file or in-memory SQLite. But Flask uses threading by default which breaks in-memory SQLite shared across connections. I'll use a file-based temp DB for tests, or set `check_same_thread=False`. \n\nActually, a cleaner approach: use a single connection per request is not ideal. Let me use a connection per request, or use g. For SQLite with Flask, the common pattern is to store connection in `g` and close on teardown.\n\nLet me design:\n- `get_db()` returns a connection from `g` \n- `init_db()` creates table\n- DB path from config `DATABASE`\n\nFor tests, I'll use a temp file path and clean up. Or use `:memory:` with `check_same_thread=False` and a single shared connection - but Flask test client and teardown could close it. Let me use a temp file for tests to be safe and realistic.\n\nLet me write the code now.\n\nLet me create a todo list first since this is a multi-step task.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0631e674f001pcEImplQfHjqC1","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","messageID":"msg_0631e3ec8001AKqWoIgYGrXtg1"}}
{"type":"text","timestamp":1788369336512,"sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","part":{"id":"prt_0631e65e8001M6dGIXnZGMXUSm","messageID":"msg_0631e3ec8001AKqWoIgYGrXtg1","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","type":"text","text":"Flask installed. Let me set up a todo list and build the app.","time":{"start":1788369331688,"end":1788369336506}}}
{"type":"step_finish","timestamp":1788369336573,"sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","part":{"id":"prt_0631e78f7001C1aqEropSg5aka","reason":"tool-calls","snapshot":"50821cb7c8519c8a5e00a58177c52f97c86127e2","messageID":"msg_0631e3ec8001AKqWoIgYGrXtg1","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","type":"step-finish","tokens":{"total":16908,"input":209,"output":158,"reasoning":669,"cache":{"write":0,"read":15872}},"cost":0.0057791364}}
{"type":"step_start","timestamp":1788369341558,"sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","part":{"id":"prt_0631e8c70001b4DiyxHAgOTC6V","messageID":"msg_0631e79470012Zkay2fXMzVP3g","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","snapshot":"e18ee26adc96367ae1c15cbf4b8537fdf2113cc8","type":"step-start"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788369364776,"sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9b398f60077ef10d","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"\"\"\"REST API service for managing a book collection.\n\nBuilt with Flask and SQLite. Exposes CRUD endpoints for books plus a\nhealth check. Run with ``python app.py`` or via the WSGI app\n``create_app``.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport sqlite3\nfrom typing import Any\n\nfrom flask import Flask, g, jsonify, request\n\n\ndef create_app(db_path: str = \"books.db\") -> Flask:\n    \"\"\"Application factory.\n\n    Args:\n        db_path: Path to the SQLite database file. Use ``:memory:`` for an\n            in-process database (handy for tests with a single worker).\n\n    Returns:\n        A configured Flask application instance.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    app = Flask(__name__)\n    app.config[\"DATABASE\"] = db_path\n\n    with app.app_context():\n        init_db()\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    # Database helpers\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    def get_db() -> sqlite3.Connection:\n        if \"db\" not in g:\n            g.db = sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"])\n            g.db.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n            g.db.execute(\"PRAGMA foreign_keys = ON\")\n        return g.db\n\n    @app.teardown_appcontext\n    def close_db(_exc: BaseException | None = None) -> None:\n        db = g.pop(\"db\", None)\n        if db is not None:\n            db.close()\n\n    def init_db() -> None:\n        db = sqlite3.connect(app.config[\"DATABASE\"])\n        try:\n            db.execute(\n                \"\"\"\n                CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS books (\n                    id    INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT,\n                    title TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    author TEXT NOT NULL,\n                    year  INTEGER,\n                    isbn  TEXT\n                )\n                \"\"\"\n            )\n            db.commit()\n        finally:\n            db.close()\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    # Validation\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    def validate_payload(data: Any) -> tuple[dict[str, str], dict[str, Any]]:\n        \"\"\"Validate an incoming JSON body for create/update.\n\n        Returns a tuple of ``(errors, cleaned)``. ``errors`` is empty when the\n        payload is valid. For updates, missing fields are preserved from the\n        existing record by the caller; here we only check types/requiredness\n        for fields that are present.\n        \"\"\"\n        errors: dict[str, str] = {}\n        if not isinstance(data, dict):\n            errors[\"body\"] = \"Request body must be a JSON object.\"\n            return errors, {}\n\n        cleaned: dict[str, Any] = {}\n\n        title = data.get(\"title\")\n        if title is None or (isinstance(title, str) and title.strip() == \"\"):\n            errors[\"title\"] = \"title is required.\"\n        elif not isinstance(title, str):\n            errors[\"title\"] = \"title must be a string.\"\n        else:\n            cleaned[\"title\"] = title.strip()\n\n        author = data.get(\"author\")\n        if author is None or (isinstance(author, str) and author.strip() == \"\"):\n            errors[\"author\"] = \"author is required.\"\n        elif not isinstance(author, str):\n            errors[\"author\"] = \"author must be a string.\"\n        else:\n            cleaned[\"author\"] = author.strip()\n\n        year = data.get(\"year\")\n        if year is not None:\n            if isinstance(year, bool) or not isinstance(year, int):\n                errors[\"year\"] = \"year must be an integer.\"\n            elif year < 0:\n                errors[\"year\"] = \"year must be a non-negative integer.\"\n            else:\n                cleaned[\"year\"] = year\n\n        isbn = data.get(\"isbn\")\n        if isbn is not None:\n            if not isinstance(isbn, str):\n                errors[\"isbn\"] = \"isbn must be a string.\"\n            else:\n                cleaned[\"isbn\"] = isbn.strip()\n\n        return errors, cleaned\n\n    def serialize(book: sqlite3.Row) -> dict[str, Any]:\n        return {\n            \"id\": book[\"id\"],\n            \"title\": book[\"title\"],\n            \"author\": book[\"author\"],\n            \"year\": book[\"year\"],\n            \"isbn\": book[\"isbn\"],\n        }\n\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    # Routes\n    # ------------------------------------------------------------------ #\n    @app.route(\"/health\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n    def health() -> Any:\n        return jsonify({\"status\": \"ok\"}), 200\n\n    @app.route(\"/books\", methods=[\"POST\"])\n    def create_book() -> Any:\n        data = request.get_json(silent=True)\n        if data is None:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Request body must be valid JSON.\"}), 400\n\n        errors, cleaned = validate_payload(data)\n        if errors:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Validation failed.\", \"details\": errors}), 400\n\n        db = get_db()\n        cursor = db.execute(\n            \"INSERT INTO books (title, author, year, isbn) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?)\",\n            (\n                cleaned[\"title\"],\n                cleaned[\"author\"],\n                cleaned.get(\"year\"),\n                cleaned.get(\"isbn\"),\n            ),\n        )\n        db.commit()\n        book = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (cursor.lastrowid,)\n        ).fetchone()\n        return jsonify(serialize(book)), 201\n\n    @app.route(\"/books\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n    def list_books() -> Any:\n        author = request.args.get(\"author\")\n        db = get_db()\n        if author:\n            rows = db.execute(\n                \"SELECT * FROM books WHERE author = ? ORDER BY id\", (author,)\n            ).fetchall()\n        else:\n            rows = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM books ORDER BY id\").fetchall()\n        return jsonify([serialize(r) for r in rows]), 200\n\n    @app.route(\"/books/<int:book_id>\", methods=[\"GET\"])\n    def get_book(book_id: int) -> Any:\n        db = get_db()\n        row = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (book_id,)).fetchone()\n        if row is None:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Book not found.\"}), 404\n        return jsonify(serialize(row)), 200\n\n    @app.route(\"/books/<int:book_id>\", methods=[\"PUT\"])\n    def update_book(book_id: int) -> Any:\n        data = request.get_json(silent=True)\n        if data is None:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Request body must be valid JSON.\"}), 400\n\n        db = get_db()\n        existing = db.execute(\n            \"SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (book_id,)\n        ).fetchone()\n        if existing is None:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Book not found.\"}), 404\n\n        errors, cleaned = validate_payload(data)\n        if errors:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Validation failed.\", \"details\": errors}), 400\n\n        # Merge: fall back to existing values for unspecified fields.\n        merged = {\n            \"title\": cleaned.get(\"title\", existing[\"title\"]),\n            \"author\": cleaned.get(\"author\", existing[\"author\"]),\n            \"year\": cleaned.get(\"year\", existing[\"year\"]),\n            \"isbn\": cleaned.get(\"isbn\", existing[\"isbn\"]),\n        }\n        db.execute(\n            \"UPDATE books SET title = ?, author = ?, year = ?, isbn = ? WHERE id = ?\",\n            (\n                merged[\"title\"],\n                merged[\"author\"],\n                merged[\"year\"],\n                merged[\"isbn\"],\n                book_id,\n            ),\n        )\n        db.commit()\n        row = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (book_id,)).fetchone()\n        return jsonify(serialize(row)), 200\n\n    @app.route(\"/books/<int:book_id>\", methods=[\"DELETE\"])\n    def delete_book(book_id: int) -> Any:\n        db = get_db()\n        row = db.execute(\"SELECT * FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (book_id,)).fetchone()\n        if row is None:\n            return jsonify({\"error\": \"Book not found.\"}), 404\n        db.execute(\"DELETE FROM books WHERE id = ?\", (book_id,))\n        db.commit()\n        return \"\", 204\n\n    return app\n\n\n# Module-level app for ``flask run`` and direct execution.\napp = create_app()\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    app.run(host=\"0.0.0.0\", port=5000, debug=True)\n","filePath":"/workspace/app.py"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"filepath":"/workspace/app.py","exists":false,"truncated":false},"title":"app.py","time":{"start":1788369364747,"end":1788369364772}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now let me write app.py. I'll use the application factory pattern.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0631e8d09001mEYnkAqaHNP3So","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","messageID":"msg_0631e79470012Zkay2fXMzVP3g"}}
