r is missing -> errors out.\n\nI have two design options:\n1. Make PUT require all fields (full replace) - then test should send all fields.\n2. Make PUT support partial updates - validate only present fields.\n\nThe TASK says \"Include input validation (title and author are required)\". This applies to creation. For updates, it's ambiguous. Partial updates are nicer. Let me make `validate_payload` accept a `partial` flag: when partial, only validate present fields (no required check). \n\nLet me update `validate_payload` to take a `partial` parameter, and in `update_book` call `validate_payload(data, partial=True)`. But there's a subtlety: if a partial update omits both title and author entirely, that's still valid (just updates other fields). But if it sends an empty title, that should be rejected.\n\nLet me refactor. I'll add `partial: bool = False` param. When partial, skip the \"required\" check (only validate type/emptiness when the key is present).\n\nLet me rewrite validate_payload to handle partial.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: the merge logic in update_book already falls back to existing values. So partial=True is the right behavior. Let me update.\n\nI'll modify the title/author blocks: if partial and the key is not present in data, skip (don't add error). But if present and empty/invalid, still error.\n\nHow to detect \"not present\"? Use `\"title\" in data`. Let me rewrite.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_063205766001AYvIuVpib2Sche","sessionID":"ses_f9ce21c9dffeUMalt2vbnwe2Vc","messageID":"msg_06320123a001a7RkmAmiuyFLNA"}}
